        "title": "fix(nvidia): use Nemotron Super 1M context",
        "body": "## Summary\n\nCorrect the bundled NVIDIA Nemotron 3 Super metadata so OpenClaw's fallback catalog uses the model card's documented 1,000,000-token context window.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Update the bundled Nemotron 3 Super context window from 262,144 to 1,000,000 tokens.\n- Leave NVIDIA's public featured-model feed values unchanged and authoritative.\n- Align the bundled fallback documentation and focused provider test.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/nvidia` passed.\n- Targeted oxfmt and oxlint checks passed.\n- NVIDIA docs MDX and link checks passed.\n- `git diff --check` passed.\n- Fresh tracked-diff autoreview reported no accepted/actionable findings (0.94 confidence).\n- Live feed inspection confirmed the current featured row still reports 262,144 tokens and is not rewritten by this change.\n\n## Notes\n\n- NVIDIA can correct the public featured-model feed at its source; authenticated live-catalog consumers will receive that value without OpenClaw normalization.\n- Existing explicit model overrides and `agents.defaults.contextTokens` caps remain authoritative.\n- No config schema, CLI, gateway protocol, or Plugin SDK contract changes.\n- AI-assisted; I reviewed the implementation and validation results.\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe bundled fallback catalog advertised 262,144 tokens for Nemotron 3 Super even though NVIDIA's model card specifies a 1,000,000-token context window. Users relying on the bundled fallback could therefore compact earlier than necessary.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe bundled metadata should match the NVIDIA model card. The separate public featured-model feed remains provider-owned and passes through unchanged, avoiding duplicate correction policy in OpenClaw.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers of the bundled NVIDIA fallback catalog receive the intended 1,000,000-token context budget. Users receiving the live featured catalog will pick up its corrected value when NVIDIA updates the feed.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- NVIDIA's hosted model card reports `context: 1000000` for Nemotron 3 Super.\n- A focused provider test proves the bundled fallback exposes a 1,000,000-token context window.\n- Existing live-catalog tests pass with the provider-owned feed path unchanged.\n",
